@startuml
skinparam monochrome true
title LinkMasterΨ — capture pipeline → NetHook join (v1.5.0)

start
:page boot (host-gated);
:NetHook arm (kernel __4NDR0_NET_API__, realm slot);
note right
  The page-realm wrap family is
  kernel-owned: one fetch/XHR
  wrap set per realm shared by
  15 canon consumers (sink
  census adjudication).
end note

partition "capture channels" {
  :DOM extraction — extractExternalHostLinks()
  (per-invocation link Set, call-scoped);
  :MutationObserver family (filtered + debounced);
  :NetHook onTraffic — response-phase media join;
  :text ingest (Route 1 structural → Route 2 net)
  with per-ingest prog Map (call-scoped);
}

if (candidate link / media found?) then (yes)
  :confirmation-HREF deprox (decodeConfirmationHref);
  :isExternalHoster classify;
  :preview thumb map (build once);
  :vault append (dedupe: seen-registries, has-guards);
  :UI overlay render (createElement family — zero innerHTML, R3 endgame);
else (no)
  :observers keep watching;
endif

partition "media resolution" {
  :gmFetch (kernel v5.1 transport — timeout-bound, typed NetError);
  if (blob produced?) then (yes)
    :vault URL mint (data-/blob- bridge);
  else (no)
    :typed NetError path — no silent swallow;
  endif
}

:export / clipboard (execCommand fallback for cross-origin iframes);
stop

note bottom
  v1.5.0 (B.1) round: link Sets are per-invocation
  call-scoped work state (cache census class); the ψ-family
  page-realm wraps ride the NetHook singleton (global census
  ledger); no interval sites survive unbounded (polling census).
end note
@enduml
